    {
      "id": "b3.2.01",
      "n": 1,
      "prompt": "Prove: if $a > 0$ and $b < 0$, then $ab < 0$.",
      "answer": {
        "type": "self-check"
      },
      "answerText": "a(−b) > 0 by POS 1, so −(ab) > 0",
      "solution": [
        "Since b < 0, we have −b > 0 (POS 2).",
        "a(−b) > 0 by POS 1.",
        "a(−b) = −(ab) by N9. So −(ab) > 0, and ab < 0."
      ],
      "langType": "§2 ex. 1",
      "hints": [
        "Use −b > 0 and POS 1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3.2.02",
      "n": 2,
      "prompt": "Prove: if $a < 0$, then $a^{-1} < 0$.",
      "answer": {
        "type": "self-check"
      },
      "answerText": "If a⁻¹ > 0, then aa⁻¹ < 0, a contradiction",
      "solution": [
        "Suppose a⁻¹ > 0. Then a⁻¹ is a positive number.",
        "From problem 1: a < 0 and a⁻¹ > 0 give a · a⁻¹ < 0.",
        "But a · a⁻¹ = 1 > 0. This is a contradiction, so a⁻¹ < 0."
      ],
      "langType": "§2 ex. 3",
      "hints": [
        "Suppose the opposite. Use problem 1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3.2.03",
      "n": 3,
      "prompt": "Prove: if $a, b > 0$, then $\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b}$.",
      "answer": {
        "type": "self-check"
      },
      "answerText": "(√a√b)² = ab, and √a√b > 0",
      "solution": [
        "(√a√b)² = (√a)²(√b)² = ab.",
        "√a√b > 0 by POS 1.",
        "The positive number with square ab is √(ab). So √(ab) = √a√b."
      ],
      "langType": "§2 ex. 4",
      "hints": [
        "Show that $\\sqrt{a}\\sqrt{b}$ is positive and has the square $ab$."
      ]
    },
